   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source video for the target video edit.\n<Picture 1> is a reference image for the color and surface texture of the new mass that replaces the bath water. It is not a frame of the target video.\n<Subject 1> is the woman in <Video 1>: her identity, face, hair, body, poses, movements and expressions exactly as in <Video 1>, frame by frame, with her hair gathered in a high bun at every moment.\n<Subject 2> is the bath water in <Video 1>: the green water filling the bathtub around the woman, up to its surface line inside the tub.\n<Subject 3> is the setting from <Video 1>: the bathroom, the bathtub with its walls and rim, the objects around it and the lighting.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. The woman sits in the bathtub and moves exactly as in <Video 1>, but the green bath water is replaced by a dense, heavy, highly viscous dark green mass with the color and textured surface of <Picture 1>, like thick wet clay, dense mud or heavy molasses, closer to a soft paste than to a liquid, with exactly the same static camera, framing, light and timing as <Video 1>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (source video editing): fully_preserved except the bath water - the static camera, framing, field of view, aspect ratio, the woman's performance and timing, the bathroom, its objects and the lighting are copied frame for frame.\n<Picture 1> (texture reference): partially_preserved - only its deep dark green color and its mottled, grainy surface are used for the new mass; nothing else from <Picture 1> appears in the target video.\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - her identity, face, hair in a high bun, arms, hands, body, poses, movements and expressions are retained frame by frame, with nothing added.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): replaced - in every frame the green water is replaced by a dense, heavy, fully opaque dark green mass with the color and surface of <Picture 1>, filling the tub up to the same surface line.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the bathroom, the bathtub, its walls and rim, the objects and the lighting are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a clean, sharp static shot in the same look and lighting as <Video 1>. No text and no lettering anywhere. No dialogue or narration.\n[Shot 1] From the first frame to the last, <Subject 1> sits in the bathtub inside <Subject 3> exactly as in <Video 1>, with the same static camera view, framing and composition. Her hair, arms, hands and movements are exactly as in <Video 1> at every moment, with nothing added. Whatever is above the surface in <Video 1> stays above the surface, in the same place and at the same moment. Whatever is under the surface in <Video 1> stays hidden under the surface. Her hands The only change is the bath water. It is replaced by a dense, heavy, highly viscous, fully opaque mass, like thick wet clay, dense mud or heavy molasses. It barely flows, has real weight and body, and holds its shape for a moment before slowly sagging. Its color and surface follow Picture 1: a deep dark green, near-black in the shadows, with a mottled, grainy surface, patches of brighter green and small warm glints, constant from the first frame to the last. It never ripples, sloshes or splashes. Its surface stays almost still, with only slow, heavy deformations where her body moves beneath it. Wherever something comes out of it, it clings for an instant, stretches into short, thick strands, then lets go and sinks back, leaving the skin clean. It stays inside the tub, below a clean, straight line, with the tub walls and rim spotless above it.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe soundtrack of <Video 1>, unchanged.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n"
   ],
